## 4. Target HTML & CSS Reference

Before writing the JS, inspect the exact HTML IDs and CSS rules we are controlling in our project:

### Target HTML Elements (`index.html`)
* **Trigger Button (in Header):** `<button id="plan-tour-btn" class="btn">plan your tour</button>`
* **Modal Container (at bottom of body):** `<div id="tour-modal" class="modal-overlay">...</div>`
* **Close Button (inside Modal):** `<span id="close-modal-btn" class="close-modal">&times;</span>`

### Initial CSS State (`index.css`)
```css
.modal-overlay {
    display: none; /* Starts completely hidden */
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
    z-index: 2000;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
}
```
* **To show the modal:** Change `display` from `'none'` to `'flex'`.
* **To hide the modal:** Change `display` back to `'none'`.

