## 5. Step-by-Step Implementation (`index.js`)

### Step 1: Select the Elements from the DOM
First, grab the three elements we need and store them in descriptive `const` variables:

```javascript
const planTourBtn = document.getElementById('plan-tour-btn');
const tourModal = document.getElementById('tour-modal');
const closeModalBtn = document.getElementById('close-modal-btn');
```

### Step 2: Open the Modal on Button Click
Attach a `'click'` event listener to `planTourBtn` that switches `tourModal`'s display to `'flex'`:

```javascript
planTourBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    tourModal.style.display = 'flex';
});
```

### Step 3: Close the Modal on "X" Click
Attach a `'click'` event listener to `closeModalBtn` that switches `tourModal`'s display back to `'none'`:

```javascript
closeModalBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    tourModal.style.display = 'none';
});
```

### Step 4 (Bonus Pro UX): Close When Clicking Outside the Box
Real users expect a popup to close if they click the dark background overlay (`#tour-modal`) outside the white form box (`modal-box`). We check `event.target` to see exactly what was clicked:

```javascript
tourModal.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
    // If the user clicked the dark overlay itself (and not the inputs inside)
    if (event.target === tourModal) {
        tourModal.style.display = 'none';
    }
});
```

